# Changelog

## [Unreleased] - Phase 2: measured detection

### Added
- `evaluation/`: a detection benchmark. Real swap histories of the most liquid
  USDC/USDT–WETH pools on Ethereum (27,385 trades) and of the NexFundAI sting
  token's market, recorded by the production ingestor; labelled wash campaigns
  (Chainalysis heuristics 1 and 2, Gan et al., Kaiko) injected into them;
  precision, recall, F1, PR-AUC and clean-pool false-positive rate per detector.
  `wash-eval` / `make eval` regenerate `docs/benchmarks.md`.
- CI job `detection-quality` (`wash-eval --check`): fails if a detector's F1,
  recall or false-positive rate regresses, or the shipped calibration is stale.
- `tx_from` / `tx_to` on every swap (the transaction's sender and target) and the
  transaction's gas price; existing databases gain the columns on startup and
  re-syncing a range completes old rows.
- `round_trip` detector (after Chainalysis's address-level heuristic, with
  sandwich exclusion) and entity-level `position_neutral` (per trader or
  funding cluster).
- Calibrated scoring (`core/calibration.py`): a hit is scored P(wash | hit) from
  the detector's measured rates and `WASH_PRIOR`; trades are labelled at
  `SUSPICIOUS_ACTIVITY_THRESHOLD`, which nothing used before.
- `wash-train` cross-validates (leave one pool out), holds out the most recent
  20% of trades, sets its threshold at `ML_TARGET_FPR`, measures the model on
  the benchmark, stores the rates in the model file and refuses to save a model
  below `ML_MIN_PR_AUC_LIFT` × a random ranking.

### Changed
- Detectors attribute swaps to the transaction sender instead of the Swap
  event's `sender`/`to` (usually a router or bot contract).
- `POSITION_NEUTRAL_MARGIN` 0.01 → 0.001 and round-trip parameters, chosen on
  the benchmark (`python -m evaluation.tune`).
- ML features are computed in memory from one query per pool (was four queries
  per trade) and keyed by trader.
- Block timestamps and transactions are fetched concurrently (bounded).
- The real-time monitor adds labels from its rolling window but never removes or
  downgrades labels a full audit gave.
- Audits use the trained model's own measured threshold instead of a fixed 0.8.

### Removed
- `self_trading` (Swap `sender == to`): on the benchmark it flagged 70–79% of
  honest trades in liquid pools. `HEURISTIC_WEIGHTS`, which nothing used.

### Fixed
- A pool's swaps were fetched, priced and counted once per DEX sharing its event
  signature (Uniswap V2 and Sushiswap), labelled by list order; the DEX is now
  resolved from the pool's factory.
- Re-auditing never removed labels, so trades stayed flagged after the detectors
  stopped flagging them.
- An Isolation Forest without measured rates labelled trades; its probability
  threshold (0.8) was also unreachable for the model's score range.

## [1.0.1] - 2026-04-25

### Security
- Replaced plaintext `.env` credential storage with Pydantic Settings validation
- Enforced database SSL/TLS (`sslmode=require` default)
- Added input validation layer (`core/validators.py`) with checksum address validation
- Added circuit breaker pattern (`core/circuit_breaker.py`) for RPC resilience
- Added hierarchical exception types (`core/exceptions.py`)
- CI pipeline: secret scanning, dependency audit, SBOM generation

### Fixed
- Replaced z-score volume anomaly with MAD/IQR (distribution-agnostic)
- Made bot detection thresholds configurable (not hardcoded)
- Fixed RPC placeholder validation (fails fast on `YOUR_KEY`)
- Added graceful shutdown with SIGINT/SIGTERM handlers
- Enforced 10M block range maximum

### Added
- ML explainability via feature perturbation importance
- Database health checks and connection pre-ping
- Automatic data cleanup by retention period
- Per-pool contamination override for ML training
- Full type hints across all modules

### Changed
- Python requirement: 3.10 → 3.11
- Dependency pinning with upper bounds
- `pyproject.toml` replaces `setup.py` as primary config
- CI workflow renamed to neutral `ci` (no security disclosure)

## [1.0.0] - Initial Release

- Multi-chain support (20+ networks)
- Multi-DEX support (Uniswap V2/V3, PancakeSwap, Sushiswap, Curve, Balancer, etc.)
- Heuristic detection: self-trading, circular, bot, volume anomaly, clusters
- ML: Isolation Forest with 16 features
- Real-time WebSocket listeners
- JSON/CSV export
